{
  "requirement": "The SDK offers this `Sources` method. Its source tools expose the\n`list_sources` command within the project directory.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Sources {\n    // ...\n\n    /// List file identities within this scope.\n    pub async fn list(&self, scope: &SourceScope) -> Result<Vec<PathBuf>, SourceError>;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations in `requirements.sdk.graph.context-tools.list_sources.fn`**\n1. `Sources` offers `async fn list(&self, scope: &SourceScope) -> Result<Vec<PathBuf>, SourceError>`.\n2. The source tools expose a `list_sources` command that works within the project directory.\n\nThe detailed result semantics (ignore rules, scope, errors) belong to the sibling requirements `list_sources.behavior` and `list_sources.inputs`. They are not assessed here.\n\n**Test mapping**\n\nThe marked test is `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[fixed_tools_deliver_domain_contents_with_mandatory_snapshot_dependencies]`. It covers both obligations.\n- **Exposure.** It asserts that `session.definitions()` returns the tool names in order, starting with `\"list_sources\"`. This shows the command is exposed.\n- **Method and signature.** It dispatches `list_sources` with `{\"prefix\":\"source.txt\"}`. `ProjectSources::dispatch` implements this by calling `self.tools.sources.list(&scope)`, which a ripgrep search of the implementation showed. The test asserts the result is exactly `{\"files\":[\"source.txt\"]}` and that there are no dependencies. So the `Sources::list` method exists, takes a `SourceScope`, and returns the file identities as `Vec<PathBuf>`. The compiler enforces the signature, and the test checks the output.\n- **Project directory.** The test builds `Sources::new(root.path())` over a temp directory. The listing returns the project-relative path `source.txt`, not an absolute path.\n\n**Other tests**\n- Many tests call `Sources::list` directly: `tests/source_defaults.rs` (several functions) and `sources/tests.rs`. They check scoping, empty and missing roots, symlinks and the project boundary, and ignore handling.\n- `agent/tests.rs#fn[source_discovery_and_its_pages_do_not_register_reads]` and `fn[source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results]` check the generic `SourceSession` tool definitions and dispatch of `list_sources`. These are marked only for `list_sources.behavior` and `list_sources.inputs`, not `.fn`. That is at most a marking gap, and the marked test already covers the subject's obligations.\n\n**Gaps:** none. No `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
